            <ArticleTitle>Auer rod-like inclusions in non blast cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1684/abc.2017.1302</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 69-year-old adult case with a monoclonal gammopathy incidentally discovered, associated with a moderate thrombocytopenia of 90 G/L. Study of blood smear revealed the presence of tumor cells presenting Auer rod-like inclusions, although there were not blast cells. Blood cytology as well as immunophenotyping allowed us to make the diagnosis of malignant hemopathy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
